Negative control for the page's identity (D1 · AC10.4-adjacent).

Prettifies the title: the header draws a start-cased alias of the composable's
name instead of the name itself, so the page reads "Client Email" while its url
segment, route name and menu item all still say `client-email`. Exactly the
drift D1 outlawed — one identity, spelled one way, everywhere. Nothing else
moves (the prop, the heading and the actions are untouched), so what goes red is
the one claim under test: the title IS the composable's own name.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: page-header.spec.ts — the D1 case (the heading renders the name it was
handed, verbatim, with no prettified alias).

Re-armed 2026-08-13 against the replay lock (`R6-23`), which put the actions
behind their own tooltip and moved the import line the second hunk lands on.

